// extended_advertiser.nv — the Host side of extended
// advertising and of periodic advertising.
//
// Extended advertising is how an advertising set carries more than the
// 31 octets of the legacy advertising data, more than one PHY, and a
// periodic advertising train beside it ([Vol 6] Part B, Section 2.3.4).
// A set is created by the LE Set Extended Advertising Parameters command
// ([Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.53) and lives until it is removed or the
// Controller is reset; its Advertising_Handle, 0x00 to 0xEF, is chosen
// by the Host.  Everything else about it — the data, the scan response,
// the periodic advertising — is set on that handle, and the LE Set
// Extended Advertising Enable command (Section 7.8.56) starts and stops
// it.  `advertiser.nv` is the legacy engine the Host uses when the
// tester asks for none of this; the two are alternatives, not layers:
// once a legacy advertising command has been issued since the last reset
// a Controller that has the LE Feature (Extended Advertising) answers
// the extended ones with Command Disallowed ([Vol 4] Part E, Section
// 3.1.1), so a program picks one for the session and resets between.
//
// Periodic advertising belongs to an advertising set.  The LE Set
// Periodic Advertising Parameters command ([Vol 4] Part E, Section
// 7.8.61) gives the set a periodic advertising interval and properties,
// the LE Set Periodic Advertising Data command (Section 7.8.62) gives it
// the data of the AUX_SYNC_IND PDU, and the LE Set Periodic Advertising
// Enable command (Section 7.8.63) starts the train.  A set that carries
// periodic advertising shall not be connectable, scannable, legacy or
// anonymous (Section 7.8.53), which is what `non_connectable_parameters`
// below builds: an extended, undirected, non-connectable and
// non-scannable set that keeps the advertiser's address in its PDUs.
//
// The Periodic Advertising Synchronization Transfer procedure
// ([Vol 3] Part C, Section 9.5.4) moves the synchronization information
// of a train over an LE connection, and the side that sends it differs
// with the role:
//
//   * a Periodic Advertiser hands over the train of its own advertising
//     set, with the LE Periodic Advertising Set Info Transfer command
//     ([Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.90), which names an
//     Advertising_Handle;
//   * a device synchronized to somebody else's train hands that one
//     over, with the LE Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer command
//     (Section 7.8.89), which names a Sync_Handle;
//   * the receiving side says what it will do with what it is sent, with
//     the LE Set Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer Parameters command
//     (Section 7.8.91): Mode 0x01 takes the transfer and keeps periodic
//     advertising reports off, Mode 0x02 takes it and turns them on.
//
// The module builds the HCI Command packets those operations take and
// performs no I/O; the program that owns the transport sends them.  The
// commands carry the parameters the AutoPTS project's BTP GAP commands
// give (autopts doc/btp_gap.txt), so the decisions they leave open — the
// advertising interval of a periodic advertising set, the PHYs it
// advertises on, the service data of a transfer — are made here, once,
// and are the subject of the module's tests.
//
// Periodic Advertising with Responses is the same train with subevents
// and response slots ([Vol 4] Part E, Sections 7.8.61 [v2] and 7.8.125).
// It differs from the plain train in three ways this module owns:
//
//   * its parameters go out in the twelve-octet [v2] form of the LE Set
//     Periodic Advertising Parameters command, which is the first form
//     plus Num_Subevents and the four parameters that describe the
//     subevents;
//   * it carries no periodic advertising data.  The data of a periodic
//     event is split across its subevents, and the Controller asks the
//     Host for the data of each subevent with the LE Periodic
//     Advertising Subevent Data Request event, which the Host answers
//     with the LE Set Periodic Advertising Subevent Data command.  The
//     LE Set Periodic Advertising Data command is answered Command
//     Disallowed on a train with responses (measured on the rig's
//     SoftDevice Controller, autopts/controller/README.md);
//   * the enable path is the same two commands as the plain train's.
//
// Nothing about a train with responses says what its subevents carry, so
// the Host decides, and what it decides is `subevent_data_default`: the
// same Shortened Local Name record the project's plain train carries,
// which is what the tester's TSPX_periodic_advertising_data names.

use hci_commands
use gap

// The advertising set this Host uses.  The Controller has one supported
// at a time (the Zephyr hci_uart firmware the rig runs sets
// BT_EXT_ADV_MAX_ADV_SET to 1, autopts/controller/README.md), and one is
// all a Broadcaster, a Periodic Advertiser or a Peripheral needs here.
pub const ADVERTISING_HANDLE = 0x00

// A start or stop that lasts until it is asked for again: Duration 0x0000
// in 10 ms units and Max_Extended_Advertising_Events 0x00 both mean no
// limit ([Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.56).
const NO_DURATION = 0x0000

const NO_MAX_EVENTS = 0x00

// The primary advertising interval of a periodic advertising set, in
// 0.625 ms units: 100 ms, what `advertiser.nv` advertises at.  The
// periodic advertising interval is the one the tester gives with BTP
// Configure Periodic Advertising and is what a lower tester synchronizes
// to; the primary interval only decides how often the AUX_ADV_IND that
// carries the SyncInfo is repeated.
const PRIMARY_INTERVAL_UNITS = 0x00A0

// Why `make_periodic_advertising` refuses its arguments.
const ERR_PERIODIC_INTERVAL_OUT_OF_RANGE = "the periodic advertising interval is outside 7.5 ms to 81.91875 s"

const ERR_PERIODIC_INTERVAL_MIN_ABOVE_MAX = "the periodic advertising interval minimum is above the maximum"

const ERR_PERIODIC_DATA_TOO_LONG = "the periodic advertising data is longer than the one operation that carries it"

// ── Advertising set parameters ──────────────────────────────────────

// The peer address an undirected set carries: all zeros, which the
// Controller ignores ([Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.53).
const NO_PEER_ADDRESS: [u8] = [0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00]

// The LE Set Extended Advertising Parameters command for a
// non-connectable and non-scannable extended set that keeps the
// advertiser's address: the event properties are all clear, the primary
// PHY is LE 1M and the secondary one, which carries the auxiliary PDUs
// and the advertising data, is LE 2M.  This is the set a periodic
// advertising train rides.
//
// The command names no address: Own_Address_Type 0x01 takes the address
// the LE Set Advertising Set Random Address command gave this set, and
// an undirected set carries the all-zero peer address whatever its own
// address is.  It is therefore the first command of an advertising set
// and can be sent before any address has been drawn.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn periodic_set_parameters_command() -> HciCmdMsg
    cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_parameters(),
        hci_commands.build_le_set_extended_advertising_parameters(
            ADVERTISING_HANDLE,
            0x0000,
            PRIMARY_INTERVAL_UNITS, PRIMARY_INTERVAL_UNITS,
            hci_commands.ADV_CHANNEL_MAP_ALL,
            hci_commands.OWN_ADDR_TYPE_RANDOM,
            0x00, NO_PEER_ADDRESS,
            hci_commands.ADV_FILTER_NONE,
            hci_commands.ADV_TX_POWER_NO_PREFERENCE,
            hci_commands.LE_PHY_1M,
            0x00,
            hci_commands.LE_PHY_2M,
            0x00,
            0x00))

// The LE Set Extended Advertising Parameters command for the modes
// `advertiser.nv` does with the legacy commands: undirected, connectable
// and scannable, on the LE 1M primary PHY, with data on the LE 1M
// secondary PHY.  Table 7.3's 0b00000000_00010011 is the legacy ADV_IND,
// and 0b00000000_00010010 the legacy ADV_SCAN_IND of a non-connectable
// advertiser with scan response data ([Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.53).
//
// A legacy PDU carries 31 octets of data at most, so data above that
// (`legacy` false) needs an extended PDU, and so does a connectable set without
// a scan response (`btp_hci.needs_legacy_pdu`): the set has no legacy bit and,
// because an extended PDU is connectable or scannable but not both, a
// connectable set is not scannable.  The Unicast Server advertises its ASCS
// Service Data that way ([BAP] 3.5.3).
pub @tier(embedded)
fn advertising_set_parameters_command(connectable: Bool, has_scan_response: Bool,
                                      legacy: Bool) -> HciCmdMsg
    let properties = if not legacy
        if connectable
            hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_CONNECTABLE
        else if has_scan_response
            hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_SCANNABLE
        else
            0
    else if connectable
        hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_CONNECTABLE | hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_SCANNABLE | hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_LEGACY
    else if has_scan_response
        hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_SCANNABLE | hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_LEGACY
    else
        hci_commands.ADV_EVENT_PROP_LEGACY
    cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_parameters(),
        hci_commands.build_le_set_extended_advertising_parameters(
            ADVERTISING_HANDLE,
            properties,
            PRIMARY_INTERVAL_UNITS, PRIMARY_INTERVAL_UNITS,
            hci_commands.ADV_CHANNEL_MAP_ALL,
            hci_commands.OWN_ADDR_TYPE_RANDOM,
            0x00, NO_PEER_ADDRESS,
            hci_commands.ADV_FILTER_NONE,
            hci_commands.ADV_TX_POWER_NO_PREFERENCE,
            hci_commands.LE_PHY_1M,
            0x00,
            hci_commands.LE_PHY_1M,
            0x00,
            0x00))

// ── The advertising data of an extended set ─────────────────────────

// The advertising data an extended advertising set carries: the Flags AD
// type for `flags` followed by the Complete Local Name `name`, the same
// two records `advertiser.nv` puts in the legacy data block, and the
// Periodic Advertising Synchronizability mode the tester asks for is
// carried by the periodic advertising, not by this.  `None` when name
// does not fit the 31 octets the Flags record leaves, which is the same
// limit as the legacy advertising data block.
@tier(embedded)
fn advertising_data(flags: Int, name: [u8]) -> ?[u8]
    let ad = gap.build_flags_and_name_ad(flags, name)
    if list.len(ad) > hci_commands.ADV_DATA_MAX_LEN
        None
    else
        Some(ad)

// ── Periodic advertising ────────────────────────────────────────────

// The five subevent parameters a train with responses carries ([Vol 4]
// Part E, Section 7.8.61 [v2]): how many subevents a periodic
// advertising event is split into, how long each lasts in 1.25 ms
// units, how long after the advertising packet of a subevent its first
// response slot starts in 1.25 ms units, how far apart two response
// slots are in 0.125 ms units, and how many of them a subevent has.
struct PawrSubevents
    num_subevents: Int
    subevent_interval: Int
    response_slot_delay: Int
    response_slot_spacing: Int
    num_response_slots: Int

// One periodic advertising train: the advertising interval the tester
// configured, in the 1.25 ms units of the command, whether the TxPower
// field goes in the AUX_SYNC_IND PDU, and the data it carries.  A train
// that carries responses has `responses` and no data of its own: the
// data of its periodic events is subevent data, which the Host sends
// when the Controller asks for it.
struct PeriodicAdvertising
    interval_min: Int
    interval_max: Int
    include_tx_power: Bool
    data: [u8]
    responses: ?PawrSubevents

// The train for a pair of intervals in 1.25 ms units, an Include TX Power
// flag and the data `set_data_commands` will send, or what is wrong with
// them.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn make_periodic_advertising(interval_min: Int, interval_max: Int, include_tx_power: Bool,
                             data: [u8]) -> Result<PeriodicAdvertising, Str>
    let min_ok = interval_min >= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MIN and interval_min <= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MAX
    let max_ok = interval_max >= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MIN and interval_max <= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MAX
    if not min_ok or not max_ok
        Err(ERR_PERIODIC_INTERVAL_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else if interval_min > interval_max
        Err(ERR_PERIODIC_INTERVAL_MIN_ABOVE_MAX)
    else if list.len(data) > 255
        Err(ERR_PERIODIC_DATA_TOO_LONG)
    else
        Ok(PeriodicAdvertising {
            interval_min: interval_min,
            interval_max: interval_max,
            include_tx_power: include_tx_power,
            data: data,
            responses: None })

// The Periodic_Advertising_Properties of the train: Include TxPower
// (bit 0) or nothing ([Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.61).
@tier(embedded)
@no_alloc
fn periodic_properties(p: PeriodicAdvertising) -> Int
    if p.include_tx_power
        hci_commands.PERIODIC_ADV_PROP_INCLUDE_TX_POWER
    else
        0x0000

@tier(embedded)
fn cmd(opcode: Int, params: [u8]) -> HciCmdMsg
    HciCmdMsg { opcode: opcode, params: params }

// The commands that give `p` to the advertising set, in order: the LE
// Set Periodic Advertising Parameters command and, when there is data,
// the LE Set Periodic Advertising Data command that carries the whole of
// it in one operation.  The LE Set Extended Advertising Parameters
// command that created the set goes before these and the address step
// between them, because this is what the Controller needs in that order
// (`configure_periodic_advertising` below assembles the three).
pub @tier(embedded)
fn periodic_advertising_commands(p: PeriodicAdvertising) -> [HciCmdMsg]
    var out: [HciCmdMsg] = [cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_parameters(),
                                hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_parameters(ADVERTISING_HANDLE, p.interval_min, p.interval_max, periodic_properties(p)))]
    if list.len(p.data) > 0
        match hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_data(ADVERTISING_HANDLE, hci_commands.EXT_ADV_DATA_COMPLETE, p.data)
            None    => ()
            Some(d) => list.push(out, cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_data(), d))
    out

// The LE Set Periodic Advertising Data command for a new `data`, or None
// when it cannot be sent as one operation.  Periodic advertising data may
// be replaced while the train runs (Section 7.8.62).
pub @tier(embedded)
fn set_data_command(data: [u8]) -> ?HciCmdMsg
    match hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_data(ADVERTISING_HANDLE, hci_commands.EXT_ADV_DATA_COMPLETE, data)
        None    => None
        Some(d) => Some(cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_data(), d))

// The commands that put the set into Periodic Advertising mode, in
// order: the LE Set Extended Advertising Enable command for the set and
// then the LE Set Periodic Advertising Enable command.  Both are needed
// — the periodic advertising of a set that is not enabled waits for it
// (Section 7.8.63).  This is the order the Zephyr host enables the two
// in, and it is the order the Controller's own state machine expects:
// the periodic advertising of a set is created with the set's
// parameters and only runs once the set does.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn start_commands() -> [HciCmdMsg]
    [cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_enable(),
         hci_commands.build_le_set_extended_advertising_enable(true, ADVERTISING_HANDLE, NO_DURATION, NO_MAX_EVENTS)),
     cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_enable(),
         hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_enable(true, ADVERTISING_HANDLE))]

// The commands that leave Periodic Advertising mode, in order: the
// periodic advertising first, so the train stops before the set that
// carries it, then the set.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn stop_commands() -> [HciCmdMsg]
    [cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_enable(),
         hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_enable(false, ADVERTISING_HANDLE)),
     cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_enable(),
         hci_commands.build_le_set_extended_advertising_enable(false, ADVERTISING_HANDLE, NO_DURATION, NO_MAX_EVENTS))]

// The LE Set Extended Advertising Enable command that starts or stops the
// advertising set on its own, for the Broadcast mode of BTP Set Extended
// Advertising plus Start Advertising, where there is no periodic
// advertising to start with it.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn advertising_enable_command(enable: Bool) -> HciCmdMsg
    cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_enable(),
        hci_commands.build_le_set_extended_advertising_enable(enable, ADVERTISING_HANDLE, NO_DURATION, NO_MAX_EVENTS))

// ── Periodic Advertising Synchronization Transfer ───────────────────

// The Mode of the LE Set Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer Parameters
// command that a BTP Transfer Receive Flags value asks for: bit 0 is
// "Reports Disabled", so a transfer whose reports are disabled is Mode
// 0x01 and one whose reports are enabled is Mode 0x02 ([Vol 4] Part E,
// Section 7.8.91; doc/btp_gap.txt, Periodic Advertising Transfer
// Receive).
const TRANSFER_FLAG_REPORTS_DISABLED = 0x01

@tier(embedded)
@no_alloc
fn transfer_mode(flags: Int) -> Int
    if (flags & TRANSFER_FLAG_REPORTS_DISABLED) != 0
        hci_commands.PERIODIC_TRANSFER_NO_REPORTS
    else
        hci_commands.PERIODIC_TRANSFER_REPORTS

// The command with which the receiving side states what it will do with
// the synchronization information the peer of `connection_handle` sends:
// the LE Set Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer Parameters command, with
// the mode `transfer_mode` gives, `skip` periodic advertising packets it
// may skip and a synchronization timeout in 10 ms units.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn receive_transfer_command(connection_handle: Int, flags: Int, skip: Int,
                            sync_timeout: Int) -> HciCmdMsg
    cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer_parameters(),
        hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer_parameters(connection_handle,
        transfer_mode(flags),
        skip,
        sync_timeout,
        hci_commands.PERIODIC_TRANSFER_CTE_ANY))

// The command with which a Periodic Advertiser hands the train of its own
// advertising set to the peer of `connection_handle`: the LE Periodic
// Advertising Set Info Transfer command, which names the
// Advertising_Handle and not a Sync_Handle ([Vol 4] Part E, Section
// 7.8.90).
pub @tier(embedded)
fn set_info_transfer_command(connection_handle: Int, service_data: Int) -> HciCmdMsg
    cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_periodic_advertising_set_info_transfer(),
        hci_commands.build_le_periodic_advertising_set_info_transfer(connection_handle, service_data, ADVERTISING_HANDLE))

// The command with which the device hands over a train it is synchronized
// to rather than one it advertises.
pub @tier(embedded)
fn sync_transfer_command(connection_handle: Int, service_data: Int, sync_handle: Int) -> HciCmdMsg
    cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer(),
        hci_commands.build_le_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer(connection_handle, service_data, sync_handle))

// ── Periodic advertising with responses ─────────────────────────────

// Why `make_pawr_advertising` refuses its arguments.
const ERR_SUBEVENTS_OUT_OF_RANGE = "the subevent count is outside 1 to 128"

const ERR_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL_OUT_OF_RANGE = "the subevent interval is outside 7.5 ms to 318.75 ms"

const ERR_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL_ABOVE_INTERVAL_MIN = "the subevent interval is longer than the periodic advertising interval minimum divided by the subevent count"

const ERR_RESPONSE_SLOT_DELAY_OUT_OF_RANGE = "the response slot delay is outside 1.25 ms to 317.5 ms"

const ERR_RESPONSE_SLOT_DELAY_ABOVE_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL = "the response slot delay is not below the subevent interval"

const ERR_RESPONSE_SLOT_SPACING_OUT_OF_RANGE = "the response slot spacing is outside 0.25 ms to 31.875 ms"

const ERR_RESPONSE_SLOTS_OUT_OF_RANGE = "the response slot count is outside 1 to 255"

// The train with responses those parameters make, or what is wrong with
// them.  The ranges are those of the command, which are also the ones
// the rig's SoftDevice Controller enforces: it answers Invalid HCI
// Command Parameters (0x12) below a Subevent_Interval of 0x06 and below
// a Response_Slot_Delay of 0x01, and above the minimum interval divided
// by the subevent count (measured 2026-10-13,
// autopts/controller/README.md).
pub @tier(embedded)
fn make_pawr_advertising(interval_min: Int, interval_max: Int, num_subevents: Int,
                         subevent_interval: Int, response_slot_delay: Int,
                         response_slot_spacing: Int,
                         num_response_slots: Int) -> Result<PeriodicAdvertising, Str>
    let min_ok = interval_min >= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MIN and interval_min <= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MAX
    let max_ok = interval_max >= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MIN and interval_max <= hci_commands.PERIODIC_INTERVAL_RANGE_MAX
    if not min_ok or not max_ok
        Err(ERR_PERIODIC_INTERVAL_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else if interval_min > interval_max
        Err(ERR_PERIODIC_INTERVAL_MIN_ABOVE_MAX)
    else if num_subevents < 1 or num_subevents > hci_commands.PAWR_SUBEVENTS_RANGE_MAX
        Err(ERR_SUBEVENTS_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else if subevent_interval < hci_commands.PAWR_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL_MIN
        Err(ERR_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else if subevent_interval > interval_min / num_subevents
        Err(ERR_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL_ABOVE_INTERVAL_MIN)
    else if response_slot_delay < hci_commands.PAWR_RESPONSE_SLOT_DELAY_MIN or response_slot_delay > hci_commands.PAWR_RESPONSE_SLOT_DELAY_MAX
        Err(ERR_RESPONSE_SLOT_DELAY_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else if response_slot_delay >= subevent_interval
        Err(ERR_RESPONSE_SLOT_DELAY_ABOVE_SUBEVENT_INTERVAL)
    else if response_slot_spacing < hci_commands.PAWR_RESPONSE_SLOT_SPACING_MIN
        Err(ERR_RESPONSE_SLOT_SPACING_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else if num_response_slots < 1
        Err(ERR_RESPONSE_SLOTS_OUT_OF_RANGE)
    else
        Ok(PeriodicAdvertising {
            interval_min: interval_min,
            interval_max: interval_max,
            include_tx_power: false,
            data: [],
            responses: Some(PawrSubevents {
                num_subevents: num_subevents,
                subevent_interval: subevent_interval,
                response_slot_delay: response_slot_delay,
                response_slot_spacing: response_slot_spacing,
                num_response_slots: num_response_slots }) })

// The subevents of a train that carries responses, or None for a train
// that carries none.
@tier(embedded)
fn subevents_of(p: PeriodicAdvertising) -> ?PawrSubevents
    p.responses

// The LE Set Periodic Advertising Parameters command [v2] that gives the
// advertising set `p`, for a train that carries responses.  The
// properties are 0x0000: a train with responses carries no TxPower field
// — the rig's SoftDevice Controller answers Include TxPower on one
// Unsupported Feature or Parameter Value (0x11), measured 2026-10-13.
// `None` when `p` carries no responses and the first form is the one to
// send.
pub @satisfies("REQ-BLE-HCI-056")
@tier(embedded)
fn pawr_parameters_command(p: PeriodicAdvertising) -> ?HciCmdMsg
    match subevents_of(p)
        None    => None
        Some(s) =>
            Some(cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_parameters_v2(),
                     hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_parameters_v2(
                         ADVERTISING_HANDLE,
                         p.interval_min, p.interval_max,
                         0x0000,
                         s.num_subevents, s.subevent_interval,
                         s.response_slot_delay, s.response_slot_spacing,
                         s.num_response_slots)))

// The advertising data every subevent of this Host's train carries: the
// Shortened Local Name record, which is what the tester's
// TSPX_periodic_advertising_data names and what a Lower Tester reading
// the train looks for.
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-HCI-056")
@tier(embedded)
fn subevent_data_default() -> [u8]
    tester_periodic_data()

// The LE Set Periodic Advertising Subevent Data command that answers
// `request` for the train `p`: one subevent element for every subevent
// the Controller asked for, each carrying `subevent_data_default` and
// naming every response slot of the train.  The Controller numbers the
// subevents it asks for from `subevent_start` and wraps past the last
// one of the train, so the answer wraps the same way ([Vol 4] Part E,
// Section 7.8.125).  `None` for a train with no responses, and for a
// request whose count is not one command — a Controller asks for no more
// subevents than the command's 0x0F holds.
pub @satisfies("REQ-BLE-HCI-056")
@tier(embedded)
fn pawr_subevent_data_command(p: PeriodicAdvertising, request: PawrSubeventRequest) -> ?HciCmdMsg
    match subevents_of(p)
        None    => None
        Some(s) =>
            if request.subevent_data_count < 1 or request.subevent_data_count > hci_commands.PAWR_SUBEVENTS_MAX
                None
            else
                var subevents: [hci_commands.PawrSubevent] = []
                for i in 0..request.subevent_data_count
                    let index = (request.subevent_start + i) % s.num_subevents
                    list.push(subevents, hci_commands.PawrSubevent {
                        subevent: index,
                        response_slot_start: 0x00,
                        response_slot_count: s.num_response_slots,
                        data: subevent_data_default() })
                match hci_commands.build_le_set_periodic_advertising_subevent_data(ADVERTISING_HANDLE, subevents)
                    None    => None
                    Some(d) => Some(cmd(hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_subevent_data(), d))

// ── Formatting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The name of one extended or periodic advertising command, for the
// program's console.  The names are those of the [Vol 4] Part E section
// headings.
@tier(embedded)
fn command_name(opcode: Int) -> Str
    match opcode
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_advertising_set_random_address()                => "HCI_LE_Set_Advertising_Set_Random_Address"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_parameters()               => "HCI_LE_Set_Extended_Advertising_Parameters"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_data()                     => "HCI_LE_Set_Extended_Advertising_Data"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_scan_response_data()                   => "HCI_LE_Set_Extended_Scan_Response_Data"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_extended_advertising_enable()                   => "HCI_LE_Set_Extended_Advertising_Enable"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_read_maximum_advertising_data_length()              => "HCI_LE_Read_Maximum_Advertising_Data_Length"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_read_number_of_supported_advertising_sets()         => "HCI_LE_Read_Number_of_Supported_Advertising_Sets"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_remove_advertising_set()                            => "HCI_LE_Remove_Advertising_Set"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_clear_advertising_sets()                            => "HCI_LE_Clear_Advertising_Sets"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_parameters()               => "HCI_LE_Set_Periodic_Advertising_Parameters"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_data()                     => "HCI_LE_Set_Periodic_Advertising_Data"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_enable()                   => "HCI_LE_Set_Periodic_Advertising_Enable"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_receive_enable()           => "HCI_LE_Set_Periodic_Advertising_Receive_Enable"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer()                => "HCI_LE_Periodic_Advertising_Sync_Transfer"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_periodic_advertising_set_info_transfer()            => "HCI_LE_Periodic_Advertising_Set_Info_Transfer"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer_parameters() => "HCI_LE_Set_Periodic_Advertising_Sync_Transfer_Parameters"
        n if n == hci_commands.opcode_le_set_default_periodic_advertising_sync_transfer_parameters() => "HCI_LE_Set_Default_Periodic_Advertising_Sync_Transfer_Parameters"
        _                                                                                    => ""

// ── Fixtures that the suites of other modules share ─────────────────────

// "PADV_Tester" as ASCII bytes, the shortened name the AutoPTS project
// advertises periodically (autopts/ptsprojects/zephyr/gap.py,
// `periodic_data`).
@tier(embedded)
fn tester_periodic_name() -> [u8]
    ['P', 'A', 'D', 'V', '_', 'T', 'e', 's', 't', 'e', 'r']

// The AD structure that name makes: Length 12, AD type 0x08 (Shortened
// Local Name) and the eleven octets of the name, which is what
// autopts/wid/gap.py builds for WID 300.
@tier(embedded)
fn tester_periodic_data() -> [u8]
    var out: [u8] = [0x0C, 0x08]
    list.append(out, tester_periodic_name())
    out
